Subject: [PATCH 150/169] build(ci): one source for the CI pytest set,
 scripts/pytest-ci.sh (gcp-juuft)

The Python pack test list existed only inline in ci.yml's "Run Python pack
tests" step. gc-ch43y adds that set to the rig's local gates (preflight and
refinery), and a second inline copy in city.toml would drift the first time a
pack's tests dir is added -- the fork already did this to the line once
(gauntlet-tdd/tests was added after the baseline).

scripts/pytest-ci.sh now holds the list and runs it. It cds to the repo root
itself, so it runs from any directory, and passes extra args through to pytest
("$@"). ci.yml calls it as `bash scripts/pytest-ci.sh` (bash rather than ./ so
the step does not depend on the checkout keeping the exec bit). The directory
list and order are unchanged from ci.yml:39, so the collected set is identical
(2045 tests either way).

test_python_pack_tests_run_through_one_script pins ci.yml to the script: the
step's only active line is the script call, no workflow step re-inlines the
list, and the script holds it. It fails against the old ci.yml.

Two consumers of the old inline list are updated to follow it, both outside
the bead's named file list because the change makes them wrong:
test_repository_consumers_use_scoped_pack_path asserted the scoped pack path
appears in ci.yml (it now reads scripts/pytest-ci.sh), and gauntlet-tdd/README
said ci.yml names gauntlet-tdd/tests.

Validation: pytest tests/test_ci_workflow.py, the full script run from the
repo root and from gastown/, shellcheck, and the red check above.
